<Base title="Guru Mandala · Yoga Shakti" description="The Guru Mandala behind Yoga Shakti with Ashish Anant — a living stream of grace and knowledge in the Sri Vidya Krama and Tantra tradition." bodyClass="theme-guru" active="/lineage/">
  <main class="wrap page guru">
    <div class="kicker">Guru–Shishya Parampara</div>
    <h1>Guru Mandala</h1>
    <p class="hero-tag">A living stream of grace &amp; knowledge.</p>
    <div class="grule"></div>

    <figure class="guru-hero">
      <img src="/assets/guru-mandala.jpg" alt="The Guru Mandala of Yoga Shakti — Ma Shakti Devpriya AnandNath Ji and Acharya Agyaatadarshan AnandNath Ji with the lineage of realised Masters" />
      <figcaption><span class="master">Ma Shakti Devpriya AnandNath Ji</span> &amp; <span class="master">Acharya Agyaatadarshan AnandNath Ji</span>, with some of the great luminaries under the aegis from Guru Mandala.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="section">
      <p>To understand a Guru is beyond us — but it can be said that the Guru is not just a mere teacher. People use the word “Guru” loosely; it is a sacred word, and must be respected.</p>
      <img class="shloka-img" src="/assets/guru-shloka.png" alt="न गुरोरधिकं तत्त्वं न गुरोरधिकं तपः। तत्त्वज्ञानात् परं नास्ति तस्मै श्रीगुरवे नमः॥ — Guru Stotram" />
      <p class="verse-tr">“There is no principle higher than the Guru, no austerity greater than the Guru. There is nothing higher than the knowledge of Truth. Salutations to that revered Guru.”<br /><span class="verse-src">— Guru Stotram (from the Guru Gita), verse 11</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>The Gurumandala</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://shaktimultiversity.com/master-detail/guru" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--teal)">Gurumandala</a> is the sacred constellation of revered Gurus — realised adepts of Yoga and Tantra. Every personality in the Gurumandala is a living continuum through which knowledge, Sadhana and Grace flow from Guru to Shishya, generation after generation.</p>
      <p>To bow to the Guru is to bow not merely to an individual, but to the entire stream of wisdom and Grace that stands behind the Guru.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <p>Yoga Shakti flows from this living tradition — the Guru–Shishya Parampara — where knowledge is passed, breath to breath, from Master to student. The practice is rooted in Tantra and the classical yogic texts, and carried forward with the grace of realised Masters. Ashish Anant is a disciple of <b class="master">Ma Shakti Devpriya AnandNath Ji</b> and <b class="master">Acharya Agyaatadarshan AnandNath Ji</b>.</p>
      <p><b class="master">Ma Shakti Devpriya AnandNath Ji</b> and <b class="master">Acharya Agyaatadarshan AnandNath Ji</b> are revered Tantra Masters and co‑founders of <b><a href="https://www.shaktimultiversity.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--teal)">The Shakti Multiversity</a></b>.</p>
      <p>Together, they carry the lineage of the Himalayan Master Shri Hayagreevaanand Nath Ji in the rare <b>Sri Vidya Krama</b> tradition. Their learning also encompasses the <b>Vama‑Tantra</b> tradition, received through Gurudev Shri Kaleshwaranand Ji (Kali Baba).</p>
      <p>Their work brings the principles of <b>Yoga, Tantra, Tattva Shakti Vigyaan, Swara Yoga and Sadhana</b> into a form the contemporary seeker can understand and approach — without losing connection with the tradition from which they arise.</p>
      <p>Through regular Satsangs, online Programs, Retreats at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@ShriAnandShaktiAshram/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--teal)">Shri Anand Shakti Ashram</a>, Blogs and sustained guidance, they continue to share true wisdom with sincere seekers around the world.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <p>The <i>Lalita Sahasranama</i> takes this understanding deeper still, naming the Mother Divine as <span class="sa">गुरुमण्डलरूपिणी</span> <span class="translit">(Gurumaṇḍala‑rūpiṇī)</span> — She Herself is the very form of the entire Guru Mandala.</p>
      <p class="living">The lineage is therefore not merely something of the past.<br /><b>It is living knowledge. Living Grace. Living Shakti.</b></p>
      <p class="vande"><span class="sa">वन्दे गुरोर्मण्डलम्</span> — <span class="vande-tr">“I bow to the entire Guru Mandala.”</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row"><a class="cta" href="/sessions/">Explore the practices</a></div>

  </main>
</Base>
